# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# Renumber rewrites a BASIC program's lines by tens -- 5,7,23 become
# 10,20,30 -- AND rewrites every branch to follow: GOTO 23 becomes
# GOTO 30, or renumbering would break the jump.  It is ONE journal
# batch, so a single Undo takes the whole of it back.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note the Edit menu offers Renumber for a BASIC file, after the clipboard
click 117 8
wait 8
expect-menu Undo|Redo||Cut|Copy|Paste|Select all||Find…|Find and Replace…|Find in project|Renumber|Complete keyword|Keyword help|
menu-pick Renumber
wait 20
click 205 268
wait 60
note the lines are 10, 20, 30 now, and the GOTO followed its target
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 10 rem start
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 20 goto 30
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 print "hi"
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas goto 23
note ONE undo takes the whole renumber back to 5, 7, 23
key z ctrl
wait 10
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 7 goto 23
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 20 goto 30
quit
